{
  "suite": "features-workflow-triage-fixes",
  "description": "Snowflake-fidelity gaps found by triaging a large external test suite against the engine: FLATTEN over a SQL NULL is a non-expandable input rather than an error (and OUTER => TRUE emits the one null row), the backslash string escapes are decoded - the simple, hex and unicode forms - with a regex back-reference needing the doubled spelling because the single-backslash form decodes to a control character. HAVING without GROUP BY forms a single implicit group so a constant still projects over an empty one, and the VARIANT path operator is not mistaken for a Scripting bind variable inside an IF body. Also covers FROM TABLE('<name>') as a table literal, CALL restoring the caller's context, numeric-VARCHAR coercion in arithmetic, ::ARRAY / ::OBJECT following TO_ARRAY semantics, a set operation's ORDER BY resolving against result-column names, INSERT OVERWRITE reading its source before replacing the table, unquoted date parts surviving a procedural assignment RHS, ANSI derived-column alias lists on base tables and PIVOT/UNPIVOT, COUNT(DISTINCT a, b) over combinations, SELECT-list aliases visible in WHERE (with a real column still winning), PARSE_JSON's tolerated deviations, and SELECT ... INTO targets surviving bind substitution. Converted 1:1 from features/WorkflowTriageFixesTest (now retired). Two Java assertions read a Double's toString - \"-3.0\" for -'3' and \"6.0\" for '10' - '4' - which the testkit's numeric normalisation renders as -3 and 6; the numeric values are identical and TO_VARIANT does not preserve the FLOAT-ness, so the suite pins the values rather than the Java rendering.",
  "tags": [
    "features",
    "converted"
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "flatten-skips-rows-whose-input-is-null",
      "steps": [
        {
          "sql": "CREATE TABLE fl (id INTEGER, entries ARRAY)"
        },
        {
          "sql": "INSERT INTO fl SELECT 1, PARSE_JSON('[1,2]')"
        },
        {
          "sql": "INSERT INTO fl SELECT 2, NULL"
        },
        {
          "sql": "SELECT s.id FROM fl s, TABLE(FLATTEN(s.entries)) f",
          "expect": {
            "rowCount": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "flatten-outer-emits-one-null-row-for-a-null-input",
      "steps": [
        {
          "sql": "CREATE TABLE fl (id INTEGER, entries ARRAY)"
        },
        {
          "sql": "INSERT INTO fl SELECT 1, PARSE_JSON('[1,2]')"
        },
        {
          "sql": "INSERT INTO fl SELECT 2, NULL"
        },
        {
          "sql": "SELECT s.id FROM fl s, TABLE(FLATTEN(s.entries, outer => TRUE)) f",
          "expect": {
            "rowCount": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "sql": "SELECT * FROM TABLE(FLATTEN(input => NULL, outer => TRUE))",
          "expect": {
            "rowCount": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "sql": "SELECT * FROM TABLE(FLATTEN(input => NULL))",
          "expect": {
            "rowCount": 0
          }
        }
      ]
    },
